# Automated PR Review Gate (Pre-Merge)

Merge to `main` only when the **dual gate** holds on the same latest head SHA:
**required CI is green** and **review quiescence** (including the arrival wait).
Neither half is enough. Human modus operandi: `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`.

**Workflow detail:** `@.cursor/rules/013-pr-review-correction-loop.mdc`.

## Bots / sources in scope

Address findings from **all** of these when present:

- **CodeRabbit** (`coderabbitai`) — prefer a real `APPROVED` / `COMMENTED` review on the latest head. A **“Review rate limited”** placeholder is **not** a completed review **and is not a hard merge blocker** (clause **(d)**). A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review on the **latest** head is never waived.
- **CodeAnt** (`codeant-ai`) — inline suggestions + quality gates. “🔄 Reviewing your PR…” is in-progress, not quiescence.
- **Sourcery** (`sourcery-ai`) — inline `suggestion` / `nitpick` / `suggestion (bug_risk)`. `bug_risk` is a correctness bug. Do **not** `@sourcery-ai review` while the 250k / 7-day budget is exhausted. Auto “Reviewer’s Guide” is not a real review.
- **GitHub Copilot** (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`)
- **DeepSource** (`deepsource-io`) — **always** comment `@deepsourcebot review` (first line exact) after opening a PR and after every fix push. Static analysis alone is not enough. Dashboard JavaScript analyzer remains off.
- **CodeScene** — address actionable comments when the check runs.
- Other automated reviewers when present (Socket when blocking, Cursor Bugbot when requested, Greptile / Codex — skip and document if trial/budget returns no review).

Human review comments that request concrete fixes are in scope while open.

## Scope (mandatory)

Address **every** item: critical / high / medium, **nitpicks**, **outside-of-diff-range** comments, suggestions, refactors, and doc notes.

## Workflow (loop until clear)

1. After pushing, trigger: **always** `@deepsourcebot review`; `@coderabbitai review` when a full review is missing/stale/rate-limited (best-effort — do not spam while the org quota is exhausted); `@sourcery-ai review` only when Sourcery has not reviewed the latest head **and** the 250k / 7-day budget is not exhausted.
2. Collect all review threads **and** every review body on the current head (outside-diff items live only in the body). Wait for in-progress bots to **arrive** (arrival wait — PR #299). A rate-limit placeholder is **not** “Reviewing”.
3. Fix or reply with a documented English rationale (rare — prefer fixing).
4. Push follow-ups; re-trigger DeepSource and CodeRabbit; **repeat until no new actionable comments remain**.
5. Do **not** merge while unresolved comments remain, a bot is still “Reviewing”, or required CI is red.

## CodeRabbit rate-limit (best-effort — not a merge blocker)

Standing policy (maintainer-approved 2026-09-03): a green CodeRabbit check that only says **“Review rate limited”** is **not** a completed review **and is not a hard merge blocker**. Do **not** wait 3 cycles / 90 minutes solely because CodeRabbit is rate-limited.

1. Best-effort: parse **`Next review available in: N minutes`** if present.
2. Post a clean top-level `@coderabbitai review` when the window has elapsed **if** you still want a real review. Do not spam while the org quota is exhausted (often 1 included review/hour).
3. If a real review arrives, treat it like any other review — fix findings and dispose body-only items. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review on the **latest** head **never** satisfies quiescence and is **never** waived.
4. If CodeRabbit stays rate-limited or never posts a real review on this head: document clause **(d)** in the disposition comment and proceed when the rest of the dual gate holds. Rate-limited is a **terminal placeholder**, not an in-progress “Reviewing” state.
5. **(b) Sourcery stand-in** and **(c) other-bot stand-in** remain valid when a real CodeRabbit review is absent; they are **not** gated on 3/90.
6. **Single exact quiescence predicate** (this is the one authoritative rule — `013`, `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`, and `docs/ci-branch-governance.md` restate it, they do not vary it). **“Latest head” / “current head”** is the PR’s current head SHA. Quiescence requires **all** of the following:
   - **Dual gate — CI half:** required blocking CI is green on the latest head (`docs/ci-branch-governance.md`).
   - **Primary CodeRabbit condition:** **(a)** a real, **non-`CHANGES_REQUESTED`** CodeRabbit review (`APPROVED` or `COMMENTED`, body proves it isn’t a rate-limit placeholder) targeting the latest head; **or (b)** Sourcery stand-in — Sourcery has a real, non-rate-limited review on the current head with all actionable findings resolved, and no other in-scope bot has an unresolved item or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED`; **or (c)** other-bot stand-in — Sourcery **cannot** stand in (budget exhausted, or no real Sourcery review is available), **and** at least one other in-scope bot has a real review on the current head with everything resolved, **and** no in-progress late-bot wave remains; **or (d)** CodeRabbit is rate-limited **or** has produced no real review on this head — documented in the disposition comment. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` CodeRabbit review on the **latest** head is **never** waived by (b), (c), or (d).
   - **`@deepsourcebot review` has been attempted on the current head** (recorded attempt — static analysis alone does not satisfy this).
   - **No active human `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review targets the current head** (moot once superseded by a later non-requesting human review or explicit approval).
   - **Arrival wait is complete:** no in-scope bot is still in-progress on the current head (CodeAnt “🔄 Reviewing…”, pending Greptile / Copilot / CodeScene / CodeRabbit). A CodeRabbit **“Review rate limited”** check is **not** in-progress. GraphQL `reviewThreads` = 0 is necessary but not sufficient if a bot has not finished arriving.
   - **No other in-scope bot has an unresolved item or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED`.**
   - **All actionable GraphQL threads are resolved**, and **every body-only finding** (outside-diff comments, human top-level review bodies, or any finding with no thread ID) **has a recorded `fixed`, `replied`, or `deferred` disposition** in the disposition ledger or a PR comment, with a documented English rationale for every `deferred` finding.

   A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review (bot or human) that targets the **latest** head **never** satisfies quiescence and is **never** waived by (b), (c), or (d). After fixing, wait for a non-requesting review on a **later** head — thread resolution alone does not moot it.

   A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review whose `commit_id` is a **superseded** SHA is not a policy block once its findings are disposed **and** the current-head CodeRabbit condition **(a)/(b)/(c)/(d)** holds. A newer real current-head review is sufficient (that is **(a)**) but not required: **(d)** covers the case where CodeRabbit has produced no real review on **this** head. **(d)** never waives an **active latest-head** `CHANGES_REQUESTED`.

   GitHub `reviewDecision` / `mergeStateStatus: BLOCKED` can still show that superseded review while `dismiss_stale_reviews_on_push` is off. That is a **ruleset block**, not a policy block. Dismiss if the token allows; if dismiss returns 403 and the dual gate holds, squash-merge with `--admin` and document it (`docs/pr-merge-gate.md`). Enabling dismiss-stale on `mainrules` is the standing maintainer fix.

## Exceptions

- Duplicate comments already fixed in a later commit: mark resolved and cite the commit.
- False positives: short English reply explaining why + resolve thread after confirmation.

See `docs/pr-merge-gate.md` and English content policy `@.cursor/rules/010-english-content.mdc`.

<example>

Required CI is green, arrival wait is complete, DeepSource was attempted, threads and body-only findings are disposed. CodeRabbit shows “Review rate limited” on this head and no real review exists. Disposition comment records clause **(d)**. Merge.

</example>

<example type="invalid">

Required CI is green and GraphQL `reviewThreads` returns 0. Merge immediately while CodeAnt still shows “🔄 Reviewing your PR…” and Greptile has not posted — the arrival wait never completed (PR #299 miss).

</example>
